Z||000000||Vlad||09-03-2000||01:29 AM||||Hi there<P>This is my first post in the forum. Hope it will go through.<P>I bought my first Fiero one month ago. This is 85 silver GT. She has 180K km on odometre and I hope to make the same mileage myself...)) I got it for 1400$ US and now I understand that the reason I got it for that price was that the previous owner was afraid of several problems that the car had.<BR>Fortunately, they were minor and most of them already fixed without big money involvment.<P>So today was the time for TCC solenoid because of the stalls at the intersections.<P>I changed a TCC lockup solenoid and by the end I had a difficulty to<BR>install back the intake hose. The problem was that side tube (near the<BR>throttle body, (what does it do?)) didn't want to go to its place. Finally, I managed to put it<BR>back, but it didn't go all the way in. Also, there is another metal tube<BR>near the air cleaner canister. It seems that it also has to be connected to<BR>the air hose. But it does not.<BR>So I think that I may have the intake hose in my Fiero transferred from<BR>another car.<P>How many holes does the RIGHT intake hose have?<BR> Mine has three. Two big ones for throttle body and air cleaner, and one<BR>small at the throttle body end for that metal tube which purpose is unclear for me.<P>And should another metal tube sitting next to the air cleaner be connected<BR>to the air hose?<P>Thanks<P>Vlad<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||AL||09-03-2000||03:37 AM||||the tube next to the firewall is the recall,that used to go in the valve cover, now the one that connects to the intake goes to the valve cover.the other tube next to the fire wall is there for no reason at all.<B>AL</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif"> <P>------------------<BR> ||||reg||1
